        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks!\r\n\r\nI'll merge it once I am at my \"main\" machine (hopefully tomorrow).\r\n\r\n------\r\n\r\nYours and a couple of several other similar PRs (for filetype which is one way or another can be a return value of `vim.filetype.match()`) made me think that initial way of getting all common filetypes (via `vim.fn.getcompletion('', 'filetype')`) might have been not full enough.\r\nA more labor-intensive digging uncovered 112 more filetypes :scream: (which also includes 'gleam', by the way). So I guess I have slightly more work to do :(",
